window.docContents[46].resolve({"/Gamma-Function/___5___5-Functional-Relations/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Gamma-Function--___5___5-Functional-Relations--___5___5_LPAR_iii_RPAR_-Multiplication--Gauss___s-multiplication-formula":{"contents":"For nz\\ne0,-1,-2,\\ldots,\n\\Gamma(nz)=(2\\pi)^{(1-n)/2}n^{nz-1/2}\n\\prod_{k=0}^{n-1}\\Gamma\\!\\left(z+\\frac{k}{n}\\right).For a positive integer n, Gauss's formula expresses Gamma at nz as a finite product of n\nequally spaced Gamma values. Positivity of n makes all quotients and powers meaningful; the\ndisplayed exclusion of nonpositive integral values of nz also excludes every pole in the\nproduct.\n\nFor a positive integer n,\n\\prod_{k=1}^{n-1}\\Gamma\\!\\left(\\frac{k}{n}\\right)\n=(2\\pi)^{(n-1)/2}n^{-1/2}.This real-valued specialization multiplies Gamma over the nonzero proper fractions with denominator\nn. The finite interval is empty when n=1, and both sides then equal one.\n\n\\psi(2z)=\\frac12\\left(\\psi(z)+\\psi\\!\\left(z+\\frac12\\right)\\right)+\\ln2.The digamma duplication law is stated on its natural pointwise domain: 2z is not a\nnonpositive integer. That single condition also keeps both digamma terms on the right away from\ntheir poles. Here \\ln 2 is the principal complex logarithm of the positive real number two.\n\n\\psi(nz)=\\frac1n\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\\psi\\!\\left(z+\\frac{k}{n}\\right)+\\ln n.For positive integral n, the general multiplication law averages the n equally spaced\ndigamma values and adds the principal logarithm of n. The pointwise pole exclusion is the same\nas for Gauss's Gamma multiplication formula. DLMF notes that this formula follows from E6 by\nlogarithmic differentiation; this file states both pointwise formulas separately.\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Gamma Function\u0009§5.5 Functional Relations\u0009§5.5(iii) Multiplication","header":"Gauss's multiplication formula","id":"/Gamma-Function/___5___5-Functional-Relations/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Gamma-Function--___5___5-Functional-Relations--___5___5_LPAR_iii_RPAR_-Multiplication--Gauss___s-multiplication-formula"}});